meta {
  name: 07 - Search Unchecked Offers
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/blocks/search?documentId={{document_id}}&pattern=Commenc%C3%A9%20la%20candidature&beforeBlockCount=1&afterBlockCount=0&fetchBlocks=true
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  documentId: {{document_id}}
  pattern: Commencé la candidature
  beforeBlockCount: 1
  afterBlockCount: 0
  fetchBlocks: true
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{craft_token}}
}

docs {
  Diagnostic, not the main approach anymore: request 06 showed the
  checkbox's checked/unchecked state lives in a structured `taskInfo.state`
  field, not literal "[ ]" characters in the block's text - that's almost
  certainly why the earlier `\[ \]` pattern returned zero results (the
  search index likely covers semantic text, not rendered markdown syntax).

  This searches for the fixed phrase "Commencé la candidature" instead, to
  check whether full-text search works at all here. Two things to look
  for in the result: (1) does it return hits, confirming search indexes
  this content; (2) does each hit's `blocks` (fetchBlocks=true) include
  `taskInfo.state`, so you could still filter to "todo" ones from search
  results instead of walking the whole tree (request 08).

  This still won't generalize past companies using this exact French
  phrasing, though - request 08's tree walk (filtering on taskInfo.state
  directly) is the more robust approach and doesn't depend on wording.

  Read-only, safe to run freely.
}
